1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,400
Previously on JoJo's Bizarre Adventure...

2
00:00:16,060 --> 00:00:17,060
Blast it!

3
00:00:17,340 --> 00:00:19,720
Oh no, the exit's blocked with ice!

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,720
And more is coming this way!

5
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:23,940
Hey, shit!

6
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:27,797
It's time to cover the whole tunnel!

7
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:30,900
I gotta find a way out of this death trap!

8
00:00:38,420 --> 00:00:39,250
What?

9
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:41,300
No, my paw!

10
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:45,560
I can't rip my paw loose!

11
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:21,920
Let's go.

12
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:57,240
All right, the sun is about to set.

13
00:02:57,540 --> 00:02:59,260
Didn't Shade say three hours?

14
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:01,437
Guess that cocky beggar had a bit more

15
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:04,097
trouble finding Dio's
mansion than he thought.

16
00:03:04,180 --> 00:03:06,877
Can't say I was expecting
this to happen, though.

17
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:08,280
Right, Avdol?

18
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:10,600
I have a bad feeling.

19
00:03:11,280 --> 00:03:14,397
Maybe it's better if he doesn't
find that accursed mansion.

20
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:15,340
Hmm? Hmm?

21
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:20,520
You see, maybe he hasn't come
back, because he did find it.

22
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:22,470
Hmm.

23
00:03:22,553 --> 00:03:23,383
What are you saying?

24
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:25,757
It didn't occur to me until a moment ago,

25
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:28,417
but a stand user is likely
to be guarding Dio's lair.

26
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:31,500
We may have put that beggar's
life in grave danger,

27
00:03:31,620 --> 00:03:35,120
if he hasn't already been
killed. What? Are you serious?

28
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:05,437
Son of a...

29
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:07,360
I barely made it out of there.

30
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:08,750
And my...

31
00:04:08,833 --> 00:04:10,197
my leg is...

32
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:13,000
That ice caught my paw like a bear trap.

33
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:15,760
I'd be dead if I hadn't gnawed it off.

34
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:19,748
I think I'm gonna hide
out here for a while.

35
00:04:19,980 --> 00:04:23,477
If I'm down here long enough,
maybe Bird Brain will go away.

36
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:28,031
After this is over, the Speedwagon
Foundation can make me an artificial leg.

37
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:30,206
But I'm still pissed as hell.

38
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:31,182
Damn that bird.

39
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:33,417
You're not getting away with this.

40
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:36,317
I'm gonna make you suffer
for what you did to me.

41
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:37,680
Just you wait.

42
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:40,600
Wait, that sound!

43
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:43,193
Something out there dove into the water.

44
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:46,380
No way.

45
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:50,280
Birds have the capacity
to dive underwater.

46
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:55,260
Like humans and canines, birds are
reliant upon lungs for respiration.

47
00:04:56,100 --> 00:04:59,557
But the average bird
has five to six air sacs

48
00:04:59,640 --> 00:05:02,287
stored away in its chest
and stomach regions.

49
00:05:03,420 --> 00:05:06,377
It's these pockets of air
that give birds the ability to

50
00:05:06,460 --> 00:05:09,857
remain conscious at altitudes
of six to seven thousand meters,

51
00:05:09,940 --> 00:05:12,300
a feat completely impossible for humans.

52
00:05:12,780 --> 00:05:14,537
Even if it were to be strangled,

53
00:05:14,620 --> 00:05:18,997
a bird can survive for several minutes
thanks to its internal air reserves.

54
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:23,740
With these advantages, a bird can survive
underwater much longer than a dog.

55
00:05:30,140 --> 00:05:33,380
It sounds like something's
headed straight for me.

56
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:34,480
But how?

57
00:05:34,760 --> 00:05:35,840
That's impossible.

58
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:40,897
I don't understand what could
be coming after me down here.

59
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:41,960
Wait a sec.

60
00:05:42,400 --> 00:05:43,440
Could it be?

61
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:56,720
It's that bird again.

62
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:59,548
But how can it survive
underwater like this?

63
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:07,880
That bastard.

64
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:09,809
Where'd it fly off to now?

65
00:06:22,300 --> 00:06:23,620
It's closing in.

66
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:25,040
But what's its plan?

67
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:26,360
More icicles?

68
00:06:26,660 --> 00:06:29,820
One, two, three! Great!

69
00:06:30,060 --> 00:06:32,060
Three icicles are coming this way!

70
00:06:46,660 --> 00:06:48,680
Suck on that, you freaking coot!

71
00:06:55,280 --> 00:06:56,900
Yes, I did it.

72
00:06:57,100 --> 00:06:58,335
How do you like that?

73
00:07:10,280 --> 00:07:13,045
The icicles are stopping
the wall from leaking.

74
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:16,977
But at the rate they're spreading,
they're going to cover everything.

75
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:19,260
No, what am I going to do now?

76
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:25,620
I know what it's doing.

77
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,706
It's focusing on freezing
the water around me.

78
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:37,320
And it's cut my air pipes.

79
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:40,111
I don't think it's trying to suffocate me.

80
00:07:41,020 --> 00:07:43,100
Its real plan is to bury me alive.

81
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:50,100
It's no use!

82
00:07:50,220 --> 00:07:51,161
It's collapsing!

83
00:07:51,260 --> 00:07:54,084
This bird is too powerful
for me to hold it off!

84
00:07:54,380 --> 00:07:57,517
And much worse, I'm surrounded
by ice and freezing water!

85
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:58,680
Just my damn luck!

86
00:07:58,820 --> 00:08:02,820
So much for finding a decent hiding
place to lay low in for a while!

87
00:08:04,620 --> 00:08:05,700
No other choice!

88
00:08:05,980 --> 00:08:08,500
I have to dig my way out! Give me a break!

89
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:12,397
This stupid day has gone from bad to
horrifying in the worst possible way!

90
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:17,421
First I lose my leg and now some demon bird
wants me flattened into a frozen dinner!

91
00:08:18,540 --> 00:08:20,540
Damn, I can't hold it off anymore!

92
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:22,072
I'm about to be crushed!

93
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:25,040
I need to dig myself out of here now!

94
00:08:32,180 --> 00:08:33,010
Huh?

95
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:34,220
What is that?

96
00:08:34,460 --> 00:08:37,820
It looks like someone dug a
tunnel down here. But why?

97
00:08:48,060 --> 00:08:50,884
It's getting ready to
shoot another ice missile.

98
00:08:52,460 --> 00:08:55,660
Damn it my stand is being held by the ice.

99
00:08:57,720 --> 00:09:01,840
I can't defend myself and
there's nowhere for me to escape?

100
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:06,680
Wait, that's it!

101
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:10,080
Either way, you slice it, it's Tarot time!

102
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:17,212
I'll let the dome break!

103
00:09:17,740 --> 00:09:21,799
And use the air pressure to catapult
me forward like a spitty bullet!

104
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:55,660
I got out of there alive.

105
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:59,649
That dumb bird didn't have to
die, but it left me no choice.

106
00:09:59,760 --> 00:10:01,000
One of us had to go.

107
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:07,517
But it looks like this
will probably be the end

108
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:10,440
for me I've been bleeding
out for a while now.

109
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:14,697
I hardly have enough strength in
my body to keep myself afloat.

110
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:18,920
Let alone make it back to shore
which means I'm gonna drown.

111
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:25,540
Why is this happening I was supposed
to live a trouble-free life?

112
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:51,340
Orchestra plays.

113
00:11:06,620 --> 00:11:10,080
Damn it, I messed up.

114
00:11:44,940 --> 00:11:46,528
Thank goodness I found you.

115
00:11:46,780 --> 00:11:51,177
As soon as I saw that little face and
those great big ears, I knew it was you.

116
00:11:51,260 --> 00:11:53,617
It's that stupid bird's
fault that you're like this.

117
00:11:53,700 --> 00:11:55,700
It attacked you just like my dogs.

118
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:03,017
You're going to pull through this.

119
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:05,857
The bird's gone, so there's
nothing to worry about.

120
00:12:05,940 --> 00:12:07,469
Try to hang on, all right?

121
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:08,430
Keep fighting.

122
00:12:08,620 --> 00:12:10,326
I'll patch you up right away.

123
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:15,800
The bird.

124
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:17,780
Pet Shop Stand Horus.

125
00:12:18,260 --> 00:12:19,700
Status deceased.

126
00:12:37,380 --> 00:12:40,615
Damn that mangy mutt, where
the hell did he run off to?

127
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:43,311
He's got to stop pulling stunts like this.

128
00:12:43,580 --> 00:12:46,874
I'm starting to get worried,
he's been gone for a while.

129
00:12:47,220 --> 00:12:48,760
That lousy fleabag.

130
00:12:52,780 --> 00:12:54,309
Jotaro, what's the matter?

131
00:12:57,360 --> 00:12:59,772
There must be someone following us again.

132
00:13:02,780 --> 00:13:05,677
Not quite, but I thought I heard a voice.

133
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:07,857
Like someone's calling out to us?

134
00:13:07,940 --> 00:13:09,460
A voice?

135
00:13:20,520 --> 00:13:21,680
It's... Iggy!

136
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:30,790
Iggy!

137
00:13:32,700 --> 00:13:34,053
What on earth happened?

138
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:36,020
Look at that.

139
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:38,600
He's got injuries all over his body. Hey!

140
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:41,040
Iggy's missing his front leg, too!

141
00:13:41,340 --> 00:13:43,400
You think he got run over by a car?

142
00:13:44,420 --> 00:13:47,596
He's not the kind of dog
that gets into car accidents.

143
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:52,668
You were attacked by
the enemy, weren't you?

144
00:13:54,160 --> 00:13:54,990
What's this?

145
00:13:55,280 --> 00:13:57,986
It looks as though someone
treated his wounds.

146
00:13:58,220 --> 00:14:00,520
I have to say, they did a great job.

147
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:04,180
But it wasn't Iggy that I heard.

148
00:14:05,080 --> 00:14:08,540
Whoever was calling out to
us was definitely human.

149
00:14:11,380 --> 00:14:13,615
Iggy did have a run-in with the enemy.

150
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:15,760
When we found him,

151
00:14:15,960 --> 00:14:17,817
he was half-dead in the arms of a boy,

152
00:14:17,900 --> 00:14:21,135
so the Speedwagon Foundation
doctors saw to his wounds.

153
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:23,660
They did the same.

154
00:14:24,820 --> 00:14:27,200
For my eyes. It's you!

155
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:28,680
You're finally back!

156
00:14:37,100 --> 00:14:38,100
It's Kakyoin!

157
00:14:39,100 --> 00:14:42,357
Good to see you, Kakyoin!
How's it going? Kakyoin!

158
00:14:42,440 --> 00:14:44,793
Tell me, how are your eyes treating you?

159
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:46,351
I'm glad you're all safe.

160
00:14:46,460 --> 00:14:47,720
We missed you, pal.

161
00:14:48,880 --> 00:14:51,100
So, they were able to treat you?

162
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:52,769
Yes, I'm ready for action.

163
00:14:52,940 --> 00:14:56,977
While it's true I'll have a few
scars, my eyesight is back to normal.

164
00:14:57,060 --> 00:14:59,119
We're all really glad to hear that.

165
00:15:04,080 --> 00:15:04,910
Jotaro.

166
00:15:12,900 --> 00:15:15,135
Where do you think you're going, Iggy?

167
00:15:16,300 --> 00:15:19,837
He may have been quite indifferent
toward humans and stands in the past,

168
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:22,777
but now it looks like he's
trying to lead us somewhere.

169
00:15:22,860 --> 00:15:26,417
I'm not aware of all the details surrounding
his encounter with the enemy stand,

170
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:28,640
but judging from his resolve,

171
00:15:28,880 --> 00:15:30,174
this is about revenge.

172
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:33,917
Maybe, but that still doesn't
explain where he's taking us.

173
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:34,980
Hang on, Iggy!

174
00:15:35,140 --> 00:15:36,000
Wait for us!

175
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:53,060
I recognize that car.

176
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:57,937
It's the same fancy ride the beggar was

177
00:15:58,020 --> 00:16:01,500
driving C-could this
wreckage mean that he...

178
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:03,520
But how?

179
00:16:03,980 --> 00:16:08,686
What's strong enough to tear a hole through
a car like a piece of wet newspaper?

180
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:11,977
It would seem as though I was
right to be concerned about him.

181
00:16:12,060 --> 00:16:14,280
He should have never been involved.

182
00:16:15,020 --> 00:16:19,380
Is it possible this is the handiwork
of the Stan user Iggy fought earlier?

183
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:23,320
All signs seem to point to
that being the case Huh? Iggy!

184
00:16:40,580 --> 00:16:42,500
What the hell's going on?

185
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:45,757
All of a sudden, I'm
drenched in a cold sweat.

186
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:49,546
And there's this oppressive
feeling of doom roaming in the air.

187
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:57,340
I don't know about you guys,
but I am majorly creeped out.

188
00:16:57,560 --> 00:16:59,960
Where exactly is Iggy trying to take us?

189
00:17:04,340 --> 00:17:06,980
I know where he's going, this feeling.

190
00:17:07,320 --> 00:17:09,060
It's all too familiar to me.

191
00:17:09,980 --> 00:17:13,280
This aura is pure, unmitigated evil.

192
00:17:19,860 --> 00:17:21,860
It's the mansion from the picture.

193
00:17:23,760 --> 00:17:24,960
We've arrived.

194
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:29,900
Iggy, you're able to find it by yourself?

195
00:17:40,320 --> 00:17:43,257
What lay before Jotaro and
the others was something

196
00:17:43,340 --> 00:17:46,317
more sinister than anything
they'd previously faced.

197
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:48,457
They would soon look
upon the source of their

198
00:17:48,540 --> 00:17:51,420
predicament and the
very embodiment of evil.

199
00:17:52,260 --> 00:17:55,820
The path that had led them
here was long and arduous.

200
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:59,017
Foreign lands shrouded in
mystery and treacherous

201
00:17:59,100 --> 00:18:02,040
stand-using assassins
met them at every step.

202
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:04,497
Each battle was a struggle for survival,

203
00:18:04,580 --> 00:18:07,580
where the wrong move would
spell out certain death.

204
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:13,380
There were tears, laughter,
sadness, rage, and joy.

205
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:15,465
The journey affected them all.

206
00:18:17,140 --> 00:18:17,970
Now,

207
00:18:18,053 --> 00:18:20,577
nearly 50 days have passed
since the team departed

208
00:18:20,660 --> 00:18:23,717
Japan on their quest to save
the life of Jotaro's mother,

209
00:18:23,800 --> 00:18:24,630
Holly.

210
00:18:25,540 --> 00:18:26,960
Everything led to this.

211
00:18:27,160 --> 00:18:29,617
The time had come to
defeat Dio and end the

212
00:18:29,700 --> 00:18:32,347
100-year curse afflicting
the Joestar family.

213
00:18:32,640 --> 00:18:35,457
Joseph was determined to
save his daughter, Holly,

214
00:18:35,540 --> 00:18:38,658
and nothing and no one was
going to stand in his way.

215
00:18:39,480 --> 00:18:41,820
Kakyoin vowed to remain resolute.

216
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:47,040
He would defeat Dio not only to save
Holly, but to overcome his own weaknesses.

217
00:18:48,360 --> 00:18:50,595
Avdol was steadfast in his conviction,

218
00:18:50,880 --> 00:18:54,939
considering it his personal duty to
root out evil wherever it lurked.

219
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:59,577
Polnareff was determined to make
the tyrant Dio suffer for turning

220
00:18:59,660 --> 00:19:03,600
him into a puppet and forcing
him to betray his own principles.

221
00:19:04,680 --> 00:19:06,457
Iggy's spirit was untamable.

222
00:19:06,540 --> 00:19:10,297
He knew his life of turmoil
could be traced back to

223
00:19:10,380 --> 00:19:14,037
a single man and was Intent
on making sure the bastard

224
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:19,557
faced his wrath and so in
other words if we Beat the

225
00:19:19,640 --> 00:19:22,677
shit out of Dio in there this
damn nightmare will be over

226
00:19:22,760 --> 00:19:26,997
once and For all that's
right and their scent of evil

227
00:19:27,080 --> 00:19:30,017
confirms that he's here he's
Hiding inside the mansion

228
00:19:30,100 --> 00:19:34,997
like the coward he is it's
hard to believe but we We've

229
00:19:35,080 --> 00:19:38,080
finally reached the end of
this hellacious journey.

230
00:19:38,180 --> 00:19:39,709
All right, man, you ready?

231
00:19:54,840 --> 00:19:57,487
The gate's open as if
they're inviting us in.

232
00:19:57,640 --> 00:20:00,875
This is totally different
from the situation yesterday.

233
00:20:13,340 --> 00:20:16,046
Now that I think about
it, if I can sense Dio,

234
00:20:16,240 --> 00:20:20,064
then it stands to reason that he
has the ability to sense us too.

235
00:20:23,480 --> 00:20:26,080
If we try to enter the
mansion guns blazing,

236
00:20:26,320 --> 00:20:29,555
no doubt we'll be playing
right into the enemy's hands.

237
00:20:29,760 --> 00:20:33,360
Before we do anything, we
need to think of a strategy.

238
00:20:39,400 --> 00:20:41,106
Careful, the door is opening!

239
00:20:41,260 --> 00:20:42,340
Everyone on guard!

240
00:20:58,720 --> 00:20:59,820
Check it out.

241
00:21:00,140 --> 00:21:01,717
What's with this weird corridor?

242
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:03,400
It must go on forever.

243
00:21:03,900 --> 00:21:05,460
This can't be real, right?

244
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:08,177
It has to be some sort
of trick or illusion.

245
00:21:08,260 --> 00:21:11,837
Listen, Polnareff, no matter
what, don't go through the door.

246
00:21:11,920 --> 00:21:16,508
Dio's probably got a couple more stand-users
waiting in the wings to fight us.

247
00:21:17,080 --> 00:21:17,910
Hey!

248
00:21:17,993 --> 00:21:19,167
Something's coming this way!

249
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:23,517
Wait, is that guy floating?

250
00:21:23,600 --> 00:21:25,188
Is he a stand-user or what?

251
00:21:40,780 --> 00:21:45,480
Master Joestar, welcome to our abode.

252
00:21:45,760 --> 00:21:47,525
We've been expecting you, sir.

